==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=roller (disambiguation)|roller}}
[[File:LilacBreastedRollerCropped.jpg|thumb|A lilac-crested '''roller''' (bird of the family Coraciidae), ''Coracias caudata''.]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|əʊlə(r)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
{{-er|roll}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|roller|roller (bird)}}
{{en-noun}}

# Anything that [[roll]]s.
## Any [[rotate|rotating]] [[cylindrical]] [[device]] that is part of a [[machine]], especially one used to [[apply]] or [[reduce]] [[pressure]].
## {{label|en|cricket}} A [[heavy]] [[roll]]ing device used to [[flatten]] the [[surface]] of the [[pitch]].
## A cylindrical [[tool]] for [[apply]]ing [[paint]] or [[ink]].
## An [[agricultural]] [[machine]] used for [[flatten]]ing [[land]] and [[break]]ing up lumps of [[earth]].
## One of a set of small cylindrical tubes used to [[curl]] hair.
## A [[roller towel]].
## A small [[wheel]], as of a [[caster]], a [[roller skate]], etc.
## Any [[insect]] whose [[larva]] rolls up [[leaf|leaves]].
## Any of the small ground [[snake]]s of the family [[Tortricidae]].
## A person who rolls something, as in "cigar roller".
# A long wide [[bandage]] used in [[surgery]].
# A large, wide, [[curl]]ing [[wave]] that falls back on itself as it breaks on a [[coast]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1907|author={{w|Robert W. Chambers|Robert Chambers}}
|title=[http://gutenberg.org/ebooks/14852 The Younger Set]|chapter=9/2
|passage=He and Gerald usually challenged the '''rollers''' in a sponson canoe when Gerald was there for the weekend ; or, when Lansing came down, the two took long swims seaward or cruised about in Gerald's dory, clad in their swimming-suits ; […]}}
# A bird.
## A [[bread]] or [[variety]] of [[roller pigeon]] that [[rolls]] (i.e. [[tumbles]] or [[somersault]]s) backwards (compare [[Penson roller]], [[Birmingham roller]], [[tumbler]], [[tumbler pigeon]], [[English Short Faced Tumbler]], [[English Long Faced Tumbler]]).
## Any of various [[aggressive]] [[bird]]s, of the [[family]] [[Coraciidae]], having bright [[blue]] [[wing]]s and [[hooked]] [[beak]]s.
# (also written [[Roller]]) A car made by [[Rolls-Royce]].
# The [[police]] (old blues slang).
# A padded [[surcingle]] that is used on [[horses]] for training and vaulting.
# {{label|en|TV|film}} A roll of titles or (especially) [[credits]] played over film or video; television or film credits.
#* '''2006''', {{w|Clive James}}, ''North Face of Soho'', Picador 2007, p. 69:
#*: I learned a lot from watching, but the part that I should have studied harder was the '''roller'''. The names of the writers went on for ever.

